{"answer":"When detect() can't determine an entry (no framework hint, no app.py/main.py/server.py, and not exactly one .py file), init() still writes small.toml — it just leaves the entry blank with a placeholder: `entry = ""  # fill in: your app's main .py file`, and `framework = ""` (packages/cli/lib/init.js:17-34). `required` secrets will be `[]` unless it happened to scan a source file (it won't, since there's no detected entry), so you'll get the `required = []  # env vars this app reads — fill in` placeholder too (init.js:36-37). `[deps]` only appears if requirements.txt exists, and `[access] visibility = "domain"` is always written (init.js:35-38).

On stdout you'll see the name, then `✗ could not find the entry file — fill in entry = "your-app.py" in small.toml` (init.js:47). init() returns `false` in this case (init.js:48), and the CLI's `init` command sets `process.exitCode = 1` when init() is falsy (packages/cli/bin/small.js:51), so the process exits non-zero even though small.toml was written.

Next step, per the skill's documented workflow: open small.toml, fill in the `entry` line with your app's main .py file, and fill in any `required` secrets the scan missed, then run `small deploy --env .env` (skills/small/SKILL.md:21-29).","citations":[{"kind":"code","path":"packages/cli/lib/init.js","start_line":17,"end_line":48},{"kind":"code","path":"packages/cli/bin/small.js","start_line":50,"end_line":52},{"kind":"code","path":"skills/small/SKILL.md","start_line":21,"end_line":29}]}
